@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the plugin class stays claudecode-only until a second harness ships a seedable plugin cache
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (_proveo_class_wire plugin:* arms)
' would touch: internal/contract/lsp_config_parity_test.go (configWiring table)
'   what already ships ............. _spec/defs/claudecode/lsp-plugins-seed.puml
'   the chain this split out of .... _spec/packages/lib/config-seeding-and-persistence.puml
'   the seed order .................. _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' Split from config-seeding-and-persistence on 2026-09-17 so that plan could
' leave _plans. The numbered chain landed. This file is the leftover that was
' not a hole in it: plugin:claudecode is wired; every other harness has no arm.
'
' THE TRIGGER, NOT A SCHEDULE. Do not generalise from one vendor's cache.
' anthropics/claude-plugins-official is baked at image build, chmod'd world-
' writable so Claude Code can drop .in_use/<pid> markers, and paired with
' home-side installed_plugins.json / known_marketplaces.json records. That
' shape is Claude Code's. Cursor, opencode, cecli and codex have no equivalent
' seed. Copying the class onto them would invent a marketplace they do not
' speak.
'
' WHEN THIS OPENS. A second harness ships a seedable plugin cache of its own —
' files the image can bake, records the seed step can merge, a binary-present
' ⇔ plugin-on rule that is not an install prompt. Then add a plugin:<target>
' arm, a probe, and a contract row. Until then the table's missing arms are
' the decision, not an omission.
title PLANNED — plugin class past claudecode waits on a second seed

component "**plugin:claudecode**\n""configure_claude_plugins""\nships today" as HAVE <<app>>
component "the seed\n""/opt/proveo/claude-plugins""\none vendor's marketplace" as SEED <<db>>
component "cursor · opencode\ncecli · codex" as OTHER <<error>>
component "**plugin:<target>**\nno arm, no seed, no probe" as MISS <<error>>
component "a second seedable cache\nfiles + records + binary rule" as TRIGGER <<app>>

HAVE ARROW_MAIN SEED
SEED ARROW_ERROR OTHER : not their format
OTHER ARROW_ERROR MISS
TRIGGER ARROW_OPTIONAL MISS : the day this plan starts

note bottom of SEED
  **One vendor, on purpose.** The cache is
  anthropics/claude-plugins-official, baked
  at build. It is not a proveo plugin
  format. Copying the class copies a
  marketplace nobody else speaks.
end note

note bottom of MISS
  **Missing arms are the decision.** The
  table names plugin:claudecode and nothing
  else. Do not add a no-op arm to look
  complete — a probe with no seed is the
  Serena shape this chain already refused.
end note

note right of TRIGGER
  **Open when a second cache exists**, not
  when a second harness is added. Files the
  image can bake, records the seed can
  merge, binary-present ⇔ plugin-on.
end note

legend bottom
  **What this plan is waiting on**
  ==
  A second harness ships a seedable plugin cache. Then: a plugin:<target> arm
  in _proveo_class_wire, a probe, and a row in internal/contract's configWiring.
  --
  Until then: do nothing. The claudecode seed and enable-per-binary rule live in
  _spec/defs/claudecode/lsp-plugins-seed.puml and stay there.
end legend
@enduml
